{#
    Shopware 6.7's Administration boot process (core/application.ts,
    startBootProcess()) only calls loadPlugins() - the function that fetches
    /api/_info/config and dynamically imports every active plugin's
    Administration JS - from bootFullApplication(), which only runs once the
    user is already logged in. The pre-auth login screen always takes the
    bootLogin() path instead, which skips plugin loading entirely. That means
    no plugin's Component.override()/Module.register() calls ever run on the
    login screen itself, no matter how correctly they're built - confirmed by
    reading the actual boot logic at the installed v6.7.14.0 tag.

    administration_login_scripts is an empty block core itself reserves in
    this exact template, positioned right after core's own
    vite_entry_script_tags() call - injecting our own script tag here runs it
    unconditionally as part of the server-rendered HTML, bypassing that
    login-gated loadPlugins() path entirely. vite_entry_script_tags() is
    Shopware's own mechanism (ViteFileAccessorDecorator) for resolving a
    bundle's content-hashed asset filename from its own
    Resources/public/administration/.vite/entrypoints.json - called here with
    our own entry name ("sw6-oidc") and bundle name ("Sw6Oidc") instead of
    core's ("administration"), so there's no hardcoded build hash.

    VERIFICATION NEEDED: confirms via reading shopware/core's actual
    application.ts and index.html.twig at the installed v6.7.14.0 tag, but
    the exact script execution ordering relative to
    window.startApplication() (a plain module-script document-order
    assumption) hasn't been confirmed by seeing this actually run - watch for
    the SSO/Passkey buttons appearing, or a JS console error, on the next
    deploy.
#}
{% sw_extends '@Administration/administration/index.html.twig' %}

{% block administration_login_scripts %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ vite_entry_script_tags('sw6-oidc', {}, 'Sw6Oidc') }}
{% endblock %}
